From 189aae115b95f11a6c88b227f4960686973fad01 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MidAutumnMoon <me@418.im>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:37:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] wildcard: no trailing slash for symlink-to-dir
 completions

When tab-completing a path whose final component is itself a symlink to
a directory, do not append "/" so e.g. `rm result` (nix out-link)
completes ready to run. Real directories keep the slash and its descent
behavior. The is_link check uses d_type with an lstat fallback and
falls back to stock behavior when neither is available.

Companion fix: the cd-autosuggestion hierarchy push inserts the missing
slash for slash-less completions, keeping real-dir autosuggestions
byte-identical and symlink-dir ones sane (result/sub/, not resultsub/).

Fork patch; upstream wontfix (fish-shell #1329 #3253 #6576 #10425).
See FISH-FORK markers at each hunk.
---
 src/complete.rs | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 src/expand.rs   | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/wildcard.rs | 45 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 3 files changed, 78 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

